## TOML Format Expected

Media blocks should have `search_queries`:

**SFW Example:**
```toml
{ type = "image", props = {
    file = "scenes/scene_arrival.gif",
    alt = "First embrace - a hug that lingers",
    search_queries = ["couple reunion hug emotional", "warm embrace doorway greeting"]
} }
```

**NSFW Example:**
```toml
{ type = "video", props = {
    file = "scenes/scene_first_night.mp4",
    description = "First time sex - missionary, slow and emotional",
    search_queries = ["missionary first time emotional", "romantic bedroom sex"]
} }
```

---

## API Endpoint Used

Same endpoint as Chrome extension:

```
POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/dev/media-capture
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://media.giphy.com/media/xxx/giphy.gif",
  "scene_id": "scenes/scene_arrival",
  "game": "two_weeks"
}
```

---

## Tips

- **Batch processing**: The command processes all missing media sequentially
- **Resume**: If interrupted, re-run the command - it skips already downloaded files
- **Manual override**: For low-confidence matches, you can provide your own URL
- **Rate limits**: The command waits 1-2 seconds between requests to avoid being blocked
- **Age gates**: The agent automatically clicks through "I am 18+" buttons
- **Alternate sources**: If one source fails, it automatically tries others
